          "https://stanfordbloodcenter.org/donate-blood/blood-donation-facts/blood-types/"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "RhD-positive red cells have the D antigen; RhD-negative red cells lack it.",
        "source_urls": [
          "https://www.nhs.uk/tests-and-treatments/blood-groups/"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Combining ABO and RhD gives eight common labels, such as A+, O−, and AB+.",
